# ── SECURITY (2026-06-28) — gate loose dev/audit scripts under /tools/ ──
# ~137 build/audit dev scripts (*.js *.mjs *.json *.py *.sh) live directly under
# /tools/ and are served publicly: CF Pages publishes the whole repo root (the
# `build` npm script is a deliberate no-op — "assets are pre-built and committed").
# They are pure local tooling — NOT referenced by any served HTML/CSS/JS — so
# they must not be retrievable by the public. The 6 real free-tools live in
# SUBDIRECTORIES (/tools/<slug>/index.html — each subdir contains only index.html),
# and /tools/index.html is the tools index, so a per-extension splat on the loose
# dotted dev-script files cannot touch any legitimate asset.
#
# IMPORTANT ordering/semantics (verified with `wrangler pages dev` against this
# repo, 2026-06-28): in Cloudflare Pages a `_redirects` rule with a 404 status
# does NOT override an on-disk file (the asset is served regardless) — only 3xx
# and 200-proxy rules override existing files. So we cannot return a literal 404
# for these (they exist on disk); instead we 200-rewrite them to /404.html, which
# means the script SOURCE is never transmitted (the 404 page body is returned).
# These rules sit AFTER the legit /tools/:tool/* rewrites above (first-match-wins)
# and BEFORE the `/*` catch-all below (a 404 rule matching first would defer to the
# on-disk file and stop), so they gate only the loose dev scripts.
# Follow-up for a TRUE 404 status: see report — requires removing the dev scripts
# from the published tree (owner decision; they are committed dev tooling).
/tools/*.js                   /404.html                                    200
/tools/*.mjs                  /404.html                                    200
/tools/*.json                 /404.html                                    200
/tools/*.py                   /404.html                                    200
/tools/*.sh                   /404.html                                    200

